---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Ofir — Build with clarity" description="Ofir is a compiled systems language with clear syntax, memory safety, and an LLVM backend." page="home">
<main id="main">
    <section class="hero shell">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <div class="eyebrow"><span class="signal"></span> THE OFIR LANGUAGE <span class="eyebrow-line"></span> BUILT FOR WHAT'S NEXT</div>
        <h1>Build with<br><em>clarity.</em></h1>
        <p class="hero-lead">A systems language with the syntax you want and the control you need. Statically typed, memory safe, and compiled through LLVM.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/docs/#getting-started">Start building ↗</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/docs/">Read the docs →</a></div>
        <p class="hero-note"><span class="note-mark">✳</span> Open source. Built in Ofir.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-visual" aria-label="Ofir code example">
        <div class="visual-glow"></div><div class="visual-grid"></div>
        <div class="code-window">
          <div class="window-top"><div class="window-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><span>hello.of</span><span class="window-language">OFIR</span></div>
          <div class="code-content"><div class="line-numbers" aria-hidden="true">1<br>2<br>3<br>4</div><pre><code><span class="syntax-purple">fn</span> main() &#123;
    <span class="syntax-purple">const</span> name = <span class="syntax-yellow">"world"</span>
    println(<span class="syntax-yellow">"Hello, &#123;name&#125;!"</span>)
&#125;</code></pre></div>
          <div class="terminal"><span class="terminal-label">TERMINAL</span><div><span class="prompt">$</span> ofir run hello.of</div><div class="terminal-result">Hello, world!<span class="cursor"></span></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="visual-caption"><span class="caption-square"></span> SOURCE → LLVM IR → NATIVE BINARY <span>01 / 03</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="section-rule shell"><span>01 / THE LANGUAGE</span><span>DESIGNED TO FEEL RIGHT</span></div>
    <section class="intro shell" id="why-ofir"><div><span class="section-kicker">WHY OFIR</span><h2>Less friction.<br><span>More building.</span></h2></div><p>Ofir brings a small, readable syntax to systems programming. Write code that is easy to follow, while keeping ownership, predictable performance, and native compilation in your hands.</p></section>
    <section class="features shell" aria-label="Language features">
      <article class="feature"><div class="feature-icon">&#123; &#125;</div><span class="feature-number">01</span><h3>Readable by design</h3><p>Familiar syntax, inferred types, and no semicolons. Spend time on the problem instead of ceremony.</p></article>
      <article class="feature"><div class="feature-icon">↗</div><span class="feature-number">02</span><h3>Safety with control</h3><p>Ownership and borrowing make memory behavior explicit, without a garbage collector.</p></article>
      <article class="feature"><div class="feature-icon">▣</div><span class="feature-number">03</span><h3>Built to compile</h3><p>Ofir emits LLVM IR and uses clang to produce native programs. The compiler is written in Ofir.</p></article>
    </section>
    <section class="showcase shell">
      <div class="showcase-heading"><span class="section-kicker">A FIRST LOOK</span><h2>Write it. Run it.<br><span>Make it yours.</span></h2><p>A small example says more than a long explanation. Start with one file and see the output right away.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/#getting-started">Explore the quickstart ↗</a></div>
      <div class="showcase-code"><div class="showcase-code-top"><span><span class="small-dot"></span> examples/hello.of</span><button class="copy-button" type="button" data-copy="fn main() &#123;&#10;    const name = &quot;Ofir&quot;&#10;    println(&quot;Hello, &#123;name&#125;!&quot;)&#10;&#125;" aria-label="Copy Ofir example">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code><span class="syntax-purple">fn</span> main() &#123;
    <span class="syntax-purple">const</span> name = <span class="syntax-yellow">"Ofir"</span>
    println(<span class="syntax-yellow">"Hello, &#123;name&#125;!"</span>)
&#125;</code></pre><div class="showcase-output"><span>OUTPUT</span><strong>Hello, Ofir!</strong></div></div>
    </section>
    <section class="bottom-cta shell"><div><span class="section-kicker">READY WHEN YOU ARE</span><h2>Make something<br><em>remarkable.</em></h2><p>Everything you need to take your first step with Ofir.</p></div><a class="button button-dark" href="/docs/#getting-started">Get started ↗</a></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
